WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.160
A few months ahead of presidential elections
in Nigeria, Boko Haram jihadists have killed

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.160
dozens of soldiers and civilians in the north
of the country.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.160
President Muhammadu Buhari is under fire for
his failure to defeat the insurgents.

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.330
The remains of a village in North-East Nigeria,
just a few kilometers away from the regional

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.339
capital Maiduguri.

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:12.169
Jihadists came on motorbikes in broad daylight
– kidnapping 12 farmers and killing nine

00:00:12.169 --> 00:00:14.940
who refused to come with them.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:22.230
They slapped me first and shot my husband
in front of me.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.240
They took my phone, my money, and my shoes.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:32.750
Then they started beating me and told me to
go home immediately.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:41.720
The day before that attack, Boko Haram struck
this Nigerian military base close to the border

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.770
with Chad.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:47.239
This video – allegedly filmed by a soldier
– triggered huge discussions on social media

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:48.239
in Nigeria.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:52.140
Eyewitness say about 100 soldiers were killed
and several abducted.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.800
Some soldiers themselves feel abandoned by
their government.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.109
Imagine, they are killing us every day.

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:05.360
A soldier will be at the war front – no
helmet, no flak jacket, not enough amination.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.050
We are fighting to defend our country – and
the generals are cheating us.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:13.770
The Nigerian army confirmed that the military
base was attacked – but has refused to comment

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.520
on the casualties.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.770
For security expert and retired Colonel Yomi
Dare, the attack is a huge embarrassment for

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:22.830
the armed forces.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:35.680
For a soldier making such allegations, I think
something is really wrong.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.320
Something is not right somewhere.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:47.650
I think it is high time that the military
authority puts up a transparent and accountable

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:48.650
system.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:02:00.130
So when things that are meant for the troops,
they should ensure that those things really

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.700
get there.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.840
And are delivered especially to the front
line.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:11.420
Nigeria’s president Muhammadu Buhari won
the 2015 elections on the promise of ending

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.360
the fight against Boko Haram.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:19.050
Despite first successes - Dare doesn’t see
a quick end to the crisis.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:24.090
Getting an insurgency to an end is a tall
order.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:28.050
Let nobody be deceived.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:34.510
Unfortunately, people want to play politics
with everything.

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:40.860
I don’t think this is where the politicians
should come and start talking.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:52.210
Because this is a war – and we should not
toy with it at all.”

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.290
More than 20,000 people have been killed since
the Boko Haram insurgency started almost a

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.490
decade ago.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:03.260
With presidential elections scheduled early
next year – Nigerians living in areas still

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:08.720
terrorized by Boko Haram are asking, who will
finally be able to stop these killings?

